Find the shared behavior that creates the two-way dependency and extract it into a third bean. If, say, `OrderService` only needs `PaymentService` to look up a payment status, and `PaymentService` only needs `OrderService` to record an order reference, that bidirectional coupling is usually doing too much in both classes. Pull the shared piece into its own collaborator:

